content.text:
I now have the full served spec. Key finding — the `Plan` schema in `components.schemas`:

```json
"Plan": {
  "required": ["plan_id", "controller_count"],
  "properties": {
    "planId": {"type": "string"},
    "controller_count": {"type": "integer"},
    "committed_count": {"type": "integer"}
  }
}
```

So `controller_count` is a required field of the `Plan` schema (which governs the plan read/create responses). The canonical v3 create is `POST /v3/plans` (vs the deprecated `POST /v1/plans`). 

Now I need to drive a plan through its lifecycle (create → commit) so it's "freshly driven, fully committed," and capture the `controller_count` the live v3 create reports. First, I'll authenticate via OAuth.
